# YOLO11n's carve: the narrow one is free on accuracy, 0.74 ms faster, and unlocks 8.83 mAP
# Host DESKTOP-CBL5NUA (Desktop 2, Ryzen 7 8700G, XDNA1 Phoenix), 2026-09-21
# Engine arms in mlir-aie-iron on Device 0; AMD arm in resnet_env17 on Ryzen AI 1.7.1.
# xrt-smi idle before every arm and after the last. mAP on the FULL val2017 5,000 at conf 0.001,
# per-class NMS at IoU 0.7, max 300 detections.
#
# epilogue_yolo11n_yolow_20260921.log left one question open: the sigmoid epilogue needs the
# attention-core carve, but nobody had checked whether that carve costs anything against the
# /model.10/ block carve the container ships. This answers it.
#
## THE SHIPPED CONTAINER IS NOT A VALID CONTROL
#
#   build/yolo11n.ignite        2026-09-15   predates the band-packed activation layout
#   build/yolo11n_band.ignite   2026-09-20
#
# Comparing today's core-carve build against a container from 2026-09-15 would mix the carve with
# the layout - the same cross-configuration arithmetic this session already had to retract once. So
# the block carve was REBUILT today from the same model with the same compiler, and the two arms
# differ only in --host-region.
#
#   block  --host-region /model.10/                                    84 layers, 1344 + 1852 tasks
#   core   .../attn/qkv/conv/Conv=.../attn/Reshape_1                   91 layers
#
# The block carve sends 97 nodes to ONNX Runtime - the whole C2PSA, its convolutions included. The
# core carve sends 33, the attention alone, and the convolutions stay on the NPU.
#
## ACCURACY: the carve boundary changes NOTHING
#
#   block carve   25.80 mAP@50-95   38.68 @50   12.54 / 30.25 / 36.86 small/medium/large
#   core  carve   25.80             38.68       12.54 / 30.25 / 36.86
#
# Identical to every decimal - but matching mAP summaries are weak evidence, because mAP rounds.
# The COCO detection dumps are the real comparison:
#
#   715,908 detections each, IDENTICAL IN ORDER, dump files the same size to the byte.
#
# Not one detection moves. That is the expected result and worth stating as such: both containers
# run the same quantized model, and the engine's layers are verified exact against ONNX Runtime, so
# moving the NPU/host boundary cannot change the arithmetic. It is now measured rather than assumed.
#
## SPEED: the narrow carve is FASTER
#
# Four arms alternating, two rounds, 50 warm-up and 500 timed frames on bus.jpg:
#
# | arm                  | G2G mean ms | rounds         | preproc | forward | decode | dets |
# |----------------------|------------:|----------------|--------:|--------:|-------:|-----:|
# | amd                  |      42.948 | 43.017, 42.878 |   3.465 |  32.331 |  7.152 |    7 |
# | block carve          |      20.246 | 20.302, 20.189 |   0.747 |  13.025 |  6.474 |    7 |
# | core carve           |      19.505 | 19.496, 19.515 |   0.785 |  12.214 |  6.507 |    7 |
# | core carve, sigmoid4 |      19.788 | 19.784, 19.793 |   0.828 |  12.540 |  6.420 |    5 |
#
#   core against block   20.246 -> 19.505 ms, 0.741 ms faster
#   worst round spread   0.113 ms, so the difference is ABOVE the noise
#   forward stage        13.025 -> 12.214 ms, which is where the 0.741 comes from
#
# The C2PSA convolutions are simply cheaper on the NPU than on ONNX Runtime's CPU, and the block
# carve was paying to send them to the host.
#
## THE CONCLUSION IS UNAMBIGUOUS
#
#   | container                 | mAP   | G2G ms | vs AMD |
#   | block carve (as shipped)  | 25.80 | 20.246 |  2.12x |
#   | core carve                | 25.80 | 19.505 |  2.20x |
#   | core carve + sigmoid4     | 34.63 | 19.788 |  2.17x |
#
# The core carve dominates the block carve on every axis: same detections, 0.741 ms faster, and it
# permits the epilogue. And the epilogue container - 8.83 mAP MORE accurate than what ships - is
# still 0.458 ms FASTER than the block carve.
#
# RECOMMENDATION: YOLO11n should ship the attention-core carve with the sigmoid epilogue. There is
# no measured axis on which the block carve is preferable.
#
## NOT ESTABLISHED
#
#   - The shipped build/yolo11n.ignite itself was NOT re-evaluated; it was excluded as a control
#     because it predates the band layout. Its own numbers on this machine today are unknown, and
#     nothing here supersedes a figure measured from it.
#   - No Ignition-side change was made, measured or proposed here. Switching the shipped container
#     is a decision, not something this log performs.
#   - Energy was not measured for any arm.
#   - These G2G figures are tools/bench_container_vs_amd.py's, whose decode is deliberately
#     unoptimized numpy on every arm, and are not comparable to Ignition's own YOLO11n numbers.
#   - Whether the same carve narrowing helps YOLO-World, whose four regions are already attention
#     only. Not tried.
